    "adapter": "Exact Solution.monotoneIncreasingDigits(n) forwards once to largestMonotoneValue(n); source byte-identical to uint20 attempt 003.",
    "algorithm_proof": "A descending adjacent pair forces a decrement in the left prefix of any admissible maximum. Scanning right-to-left propagates this requirement through equal/higher preceding digits. The leftmost corrected digit fixes a smaller prefix; filling its remaining suffix with 9 maximizes the admissible number. An unchanged prefix is nondecreasing; zero and leading-zero reconstruction work generally. No expected-value branches.",
    "numeric": "Canonical ASCII decimal inputs of 1..1024 digits including zero; unsafe values become BigInt, safe values Number. No scientific notation at the safe Number bound. Digits remain integers 0..9. Exact BigInt reconstruction precedes safe-bound test; Number conversion only for result<=2^53-1. Result never exceeds input.",
    "roles": "targetValue input scalar; characters decimal character list; character individual ASCII digit; digitValues mutable local digit array; digitIndex scan index; suffixIndex leftmost suffix needing maximal fill; resultText reconstructed decimal; resultValue exact scalar. Helper meaning and explicit role mapping match source.",
    "mutation_alias": "Only fresh local arrays mutate. Primitive input has no mutable object aliases. Raw observations are checked against original host arguments and runtime type before unchanged judge scoring.",
    "scope": "Distinct resource-bounded uint1024 transport, not legacy Number-interface qualification or implicit 670/633 policy expansion."
  },
